module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.firmware_reflash_resets_the_bmc_credential_it_needs

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import std.decl_ref { decl_ref }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { RecurringFailureMode }

data firmware_reflash_resets_the_bmc_credential_it_needs: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "firmware_reflash_resets_the_bmc_credential_it_needs" as NonEmptyStr,

  receipts: [
    "a BMC firmware reflash silently resets the controller's account table: the managed credential every later step authenticates with is erased and the vendor's published factory credential is re-enabled at administrator privilege, while the controller answers normally. A process that treats an answering BMC as a converged one proceeds either with a credential that no longer exists or, worse, by falling back to the factory one, and the host sits on the network with a published default password.",

    "RECEIPT, 2026-10-02, mtcollins1 manual firmware run from srv1 (session eager-gull-22): hpm upgrade of MegaRAC BMC 0.32 -> 0.45.3 succeeded with exit 0 and the BMC rebooted itself and answered; user 3 `gunbc` (gunbc.secret_provision mtcollins1_bmc_gunbc_secret_ref) was gone and admin/admin was enabled at ADMINISTRATOR. Restored by hand: user name and password from the SecretRef, channel access privilege 4, enable, SOL payload enable, factory admin back to NO ACCESS.",

    "SECOND RECEIPT, same run: the hand restore was itself incomplete in two ways an answering BMC hides. Factory admin was closed on LAN channel 1 only and kept ADMINISTRATOR on channels 2 and 3, and `gunbc` came back without its Redfish role (extended privilege 256, Redfish AccessDenied). So the readback that closes the window is per channel and per surface: gunbc.machine_intake_bmc_secure's census refuses a published credential accepted on ANY addressable LAN channel, and the convergence adds a rights receipt beside it (BmcCredentialReestablishment).",

    "THIRD RECEIPT, 2026-10-03, same machine: the reset had also dropped the managed user's KVM and VMEDIA rights (web /api/settings/users kvm 0, vmedia 0) and left ADMINISTRATOR on LAN channel 1 only (channels 7 and 8: none). Restored with `channel setaccess 7|8 3 privilege=4` and a web user PUT kvm=1 vmedia=1. Redfish stayed refused (401, also via SessionService) after every IPMI and web command, so Redfish authorization is a separate store. The readback that closes the window is therefore a receipt of EVERY right the boot workflow uses (gunbc.fleet.mtcollins_firmware_converge mtcollins1_required_managed_rights), bound to this endpoint, account and post-flash time, never one IPMI session.",

    "FOURTH RECEIPT, 2026-10-03: the reset also wiped remote-media configuration (remote_media_support 0, empty server/path/share, mount_cd 0), so the boot run refused at media_attach (run 37099727839). The restoring PUT /api/settings/media/general returned code 16425 yet applied (cd_error_code 0, 15 images enumerated), so the re-provision readback is the images the controller enumerates, never the PUT status (gunbc.fleet.mtcollins_firmware_converge RemoteMediaReceipt).",

    "RUNG found at 1, mitigatable (an operator noticed). Lifted by gunbc.fleet.mtcollins_firmware_converge to 2 for that convergence: a step whose credential_effect_of is InvalidatesBmcCredential does not ground until a sealed gunbc.machine_intake_bmc_secure BmcSecureStanding at a LATER epoch is recorded, the window in between is the typed FirmwareCredentialReprovisionDue state, and any later step recorded inside it refuses (test.claim.mtcollins_firmware_converge_witness step_inside_the_factory_credential_window_refuses). ATTAINABLE CEILING 2: whether a given image resets the table is an external fact observed per image, so it remains a declared per-target effect, never derivable. NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER: the same declaration on every other BMC-image flash route in the fleet (the AsRock OpenBMC UpdateService push), which today carries no credential effect at all.",
  ],

  evidence: [
    decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.fleet.mtcollins_firmware_converge", decl_name: "credential_effect_of"),
  ],
}
